  <section class="hub-sec hub-narrow" aria-labelledby="h-t">
    <h2 id="h-t">The female body shapes at a glance</h2>
    <p>Body shape compares your bust, waist and hips. Figures are from a large U.S. study of women&rsquo;s body scans; the exact formulas are on the <a href="/">body type calculator</a>.</p>
    <div class="tp-tablewrap"><table class="tp-table"><caption>Female body shapes: what they look like and how common they are</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Shape</th><th scope="col">What it looks like</th><th scope="col">How common</th><th scope="col">Guide</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Rectangle</th><td>Bust, waist and hips fairly similar; little waist definition</td><td>About 46%</td><td><a href="/">Calculator</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pear</th><td>Hips clearly wider than bust and shoulders</td><td>About 20%</td><td><a href="/pear-body-shape/">Pear guide</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Apple</th><td>Fuller through the middle; waist close to bust and hips</td><td>About 14%</td><td><a href="/apple-body-shape/">Apple guide</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Hourglass</th><td>Bust and hips balanced with a well-defined waist</td><td>About 8%</td><td><a href="/hourglass-body-shape/">Hourglass guide</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Top hourglass</th><td>Defined waist with a fuller bust</td><td>Less common</td><td><a href="/hourglass-body-shape/">Hourglass guide</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Bottom hourglass</th><td>Defined waist with fuller hips</td><td>Less common</td><td><a href="/hourglass-body-shape/">Hourglass guide</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Inverted triangle</th><td>Shoulders and bust wider than hips</td><td>Less common</td><td><a href="/inverted-triangle-body-shape/">Inverted triangle guide</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p>Men are usually grouped into five shapes (trapezoid, inverted triangle, rectangle, triangle and oval), based on chest, waist and hips. The <a href="/male-body-type-calculator/">male body type calculator</a> explains each one.</p>
